&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a SE II Engineer, Platform you will play a critical role helping to advance Ripple&#39;s production infrastructure and release pipelines. Infrastructure Engineers at Ripple are a hybrid of systems and software engineers who support the design and lifecycle of our hosted products. You will work closely with product engineers to support their infrastructure needs, ideally in a self-service environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform features across compute, authentication, service discovery, observability, and redundancy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement architectural solutions under the guidance of senior engineers, with a growing awareness of tradeoffs between scale, cost, and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and mentor junior engineers through code reviews and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help deploy and maintain Ripple&#39;s multi-region, multi-provider service platforms with a focus on security and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve tooling for automation, monitoring, and instrumentation to reduce operational friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform and application lifecycle services, working toward automated, data-driven workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in discussions around scalable, maintainable, and cost-effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and apply DevOps and GitOps principles in your day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s and/or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–6 years of relevant work experience with development background in Go, Python, or Java, with a good understanding of software engineering best practices and system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud providers like AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of orchestration platforms (Kubernetes, Rancher) and containerization technologies for deploying and managing distributed services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to deployment pipelines using common CI/CD tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Infrastructure-as-Code tools such as Terraform or CloudFormation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Observability platforms leveraging Prometheus and OpenTelemetry, with an interest in building instrumentation patterns and monitoring SLOs/SLIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player with a customer service orientation and a willingness to build relationships across teams and cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills — written, verbal, and interpersonal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
