descriptions.job-006u2z2:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bridge is building financial infrastructure that makes money more programmable and global. The Financial Partnerships team develops the ecosystem that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across Bridge and Stripe to develop strategic relationships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners. These partnerships support reserve management, liquidity, distribution, and card-related products for both businesses and their shared customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior Partnership Development Manager, you will define and execute the financial-partnership strategy that powers Bridge and Stripe’s stablecoin products and financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a strategic ecosystem of financial-partner relationships across markets. You will turn market insight into durable, high-impact partnerships, from strategy and negotiation through launch, expansion, and ongoing performance management. You will work directly with senior Stripe leaders and external executives to make investment tradeoffs, align priorities, and shape long-term product and partnership strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead multi-year partnership strategy across reserves, liquidity, distribution, card-related products, and the stablecoin ecosystem, using market and commercial insight to shape Bridge and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a strategic financial-partner ecosystem across markets, including partnership health, commercial performance, executive alignment, escalations, and expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, evaluate, structure, negotiate, and lead high-impact partnerships with banks, exchanges, asset managers, liquidity providers, and stablecoin ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set end-to-end deal strategy for complex, novel, or multi-market partnerships with material financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead company-level tradeoffs across partner economics, customer needs, product requirements, operational readiness, risk, and long-term strategic value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Treasury, Legal, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Finance, Engineering, and go-to-market teams to set requirements, align senior stakeholders, and execute shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a differentiated point of view on financial services and digital assets, represent Stripe and Bridge with senior external stakeholders, and share expertise that strengthens the broader Partnerships organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategic finance, treasury, or a related field, including ownership of complex, high-impact external partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently set partnership strategy, influence senior executives, and drive cross-functional alignment on ambiguous, high-stakes company priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of structuring, negotiating, and managing high-value, multi-year partnerships with material strategic, financial, product, operational, or regulatory implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience working with financial institutions or infrastructure providers, such as banks, exchanges, asset managers, market makers, liquidity providers, payments companies, or stablecoin ecosystem participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment and experience leading both commercial and technical partnership conversations with senior internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in stablecoins, crypto, card issuing, or stablecoin-linked card programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategy across multiple markets or partner types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a company with industry groups, at conferences, or with senior external executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or guiding peers on partnership strategy, complex negotiations, or cross-functional execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-066xolq:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Treasury Operations Analyst II on the Treasury Operations team within Finance, you&#39;ll own the day-to-day administration of Coinbase&#39;s banking relationships, ensuring accounts are opened, maintained, and closed in compliance with internal policies and regulatory requirements. You&#39;ll play a critical role in safeguarding operational integrity by managing user access controls and conducting KYC reviews across our banking partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end lifecycle of bank account administration, including opening new accounts, maintaining existing accounts, and executing account closures across global banking partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute user access provisioning and de-provisioning for banking platforms, ensuring appropriate controls and audit trails are maintained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform KYC reviews and documentation gathering to satisfy banking partner requirements and regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Compliance, Legal, and Finance teams to ensure all banking activities align with internal policies and external regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support process documentation and improvement initiatives to scale Treasury Ops workflows as Coinbase grows its banking footprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in treasury operations, banking operations, or financial operations with direct exposure to bank account administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience executing KYC documentation processes and managing banking partner requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage user access controls across financial platforms with strong attention to audit and compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with banking regulations and anti-money laundering (AML) frameworks relevant to account administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
